#!/usr/bin/ruby
# frozen_string_literal: true

# check-inbox-registry — assert this machine's Athena Inbox tenancy registry
# matches the committed source of truth AS IT LANDED, and say which entry
# drifted when it does not.
#
# Why it exists: the registry (`$ATHENA_INBOX_ROOT/projects/<project>.json`) is
# untracked machine-local state, and the contract defines a missing entry as
# ZERO CHANNELS, EXIT 0, NO ERROR. So a clobbered or deleted entry is a
# silently dead inbox — no diff, no `git` undo, nothing detecting it. That is
# the 2026-09-17 hook-clobber class, and the contract's *Provisioning* section
# makes the fix a MUST on the tooling: a committed source of truth
# (ai/inbox/registry.json), an idempotent installer
# (scripts/setup-inbox-registry), and THIS check — one that runs unprompted, in
# the harness gate, because a diagnostic somebody has to think of running is not
# a check.
#
# Read-only, always. It never creates, repairs, or touches anything, including
# on the failure path; repair is the installer's job.
#
# THE BAR IS THE REGISTRY THAT LANDED, NOT THE BRANCH'S (DND-792, folded into
# DND-743 with the same fix for check-hooks-registered). The entries the live
# registry MUST hold are ai/inbox/registry.json as it landed on origin's main
# (ai/lib/landed.rb, which also honours harness-gate's pin). It used to be the
# branch's own copy, which broke both ways:
#   - a branch that ADDED an entry or a channel failed until the live registry
#     was provisioned with it: machine state became a precondition of reviewing
#     code, and the only route to green was installing what had not landed;
#   - a branch that REMOVED or edited a landed entry lowered its own bar, so real
#     drift on main passed. See ~/dev/custom/CLAUDE.md -> "A check's own bar
#     must not live in the diff it is checking".
# The bar is origin/main's TIP, not the union with merge-base(HEAD, origin/main)
# that the other Landed callers take. An entry is matched byte for byte, so a
# live file can match only one version of it: the one the main checkout's
# installer writes, which is the tip's. The merge-base adds no protection here:
# the tip is already proven on origin, and no branch can move it.
#
# So the check reports, in order:
#   1. MALFORMED BRANCH REGISTRY (exit 2): this checkout's registry.json fails
#      the rules the installer applies. A code error in the diff.
#   2. COULD NOT MEASURE (exit 3): origin unreachable, a local origin/main that
#      disagrees with origin, or a malformed LANDED registry. Never a pass.
#   3. DRIFT (exit 1): a landed entry that is missing, malformed,
#      mis-permissioned, or edited away from the landed text; or a lost root on
#      a machine where a landed entry's repo is checked out.
#   4. PENDING: what this branch adds, retires or edits in registry.json. Named,
#      never a failure: it is provisioned after it lands, from the main checkout.
#   5. AHEAD OF THE PINNED BAR (DND-1552): under harness-gate the bar is
#      origin's main as of the gate start. When an entry drifts from it, and
#      origin's main has since moved past the pin, a live entry that equals
#      exactly what the NEWER origin/main declares for that file is measured
#      against the newer declaration instead, and named. Its mode, file type
#      and repo identity are still checked. A live entry that equals neither
#      declaration is drift, as before; so is every other problem. The newer
#      declaration is read from git (ai/lib/landed.rb, Landed.newer_tip), never
#      from the working tree, and only after the pinned bar found drift.
#
# Environment-safe, like check-hooks-registered: if the inbox root does not
# exist and no LANDED entry's repo is checked out here, this machine does not
# run the facility (a fresh checkout, a CI or agent environment with a different
# HOME, a container), there is nothing to assert, and it PASSES with a note. It
# still needs origin to say which entries landed: a machine that cannot reach
# origin gets exit 3, the same as every other landed-bar check in the gate.
#
# What it never does: read, name, or otherwise surface an entry the committed
# list does not declare. An unrelated tenant's file in projects/ is left
# completely alone — the installer's anti-clobber property has a check that
# matches it.
#
# Deliberately gem-free (stdlib only); run with bare `ruby`.
#
# Usage:
#   ai/bin/check-inbox-registry              assert the live registry matches
#   ai/bin/check-inbox-registry --self-test  verify the checker's own logic
#
# Environment: ATHENA_INBOX_ROOT (default ~/.local/share/athena) selects the
# root. ATHENA_INBOX_REGISTRY is a TEST SEAM that replaces only the BRANCH
# registry (validation and pending); the landed bar is always read from origin,
# so no environment variable can lower it.
#
# Exit codes: 0 ok / not-this-environment · 1 drift · 2 this branch's
# registry.json is missing or malformed · 3 could not measure the landed bar

require_relative "../inbox/lib/registry"
require_relative "../lib/landed"

REGISTRY_REL    = "ai/inbox/registry.json"
EXIT_OK         = 0
EXIT_FAIL       = 1
EXIT_MALFORMED  = 2
EXIT_UNMEASURED = 3

# The entries that LANDED: ai/inbox/registry.json at origin/main's tip (see
# "THE BAR IS THE REGISTRY THAT LANDED" above for why the tip alone). Returns
# [description, entries]. Raises Landed::Unreadable (a malformed landed
# registry included, carrying every probe) or Landed::Mismatch. Empty entries
# when the tip has no registry file at all.
def landed_entries(root = InboxRegistry.repo_dir)
  pts, probes = Landed.points(root)
  label, sha = pts.first
  begin
    text = Landed.file_at(root, sha, REGISTRY_REL, label)
    entries = text ? InboxRegistry.parse(text, "#{REGISTRY_REL} @ #{label} #{sha[0, 12]}") : []
  rescue InboxRegistry::Error => e
    raise Landed::Unreadable.new(probes + [[label, e.message]])
  rescue Landed::Unreadable => e
    raise Landed::Unreadable.new(probes + e.probes)
  end
  ["landed #{REGISTRY_REL} (#{label} @ #{sha[0, 12]})", entries]
end

# The landed bar as [description, entries], or [nil, lines] when it could not
# be measured (lines explain why).
def measure_landed(landed)
  landed.call
rescue Landed::Unreadable => e
  [nil, Landed.unreadable_lines("inbox registry", e.probes)]
rescue Landed::Mismatch => e
  [nil, Landed.mismatch_lines(e.local, e.remote, e.source)]
end

# What this branch's registry changes relative to the landed one, one line per
# entry file. None of it is required of the live registry until it lands.
def pending_changes(branch, landed)
  have = landed.to_h { |p| [p["file"], p["entry"]] }
  want = branch.to_h { |p| [p["file"], p["entry"]] }
  lines = (want.keys - have.keys).map do |file|
    names = channel_names(want[file])
    "#{file}: a new entry (channels: #{names.empty? ? 'none' : names.join(', ')})"
  end
  (have.keys - want.keys).each do |file|
    lines << "#{file}: retired on this branch (the landed entry is still required until this lands)"
  end
  (want.keys & have.keys).each do |file|
    lines << "#{file}: #{entry_change(have[file], want[file])}" unless want[file] == have[file]
  end
  lines
end

def channels_of(entry)
  entry["channels"].is_a?(Hash) ? entry["channels"] : {}
end

def channel_names(entry)
  channels_of(entry).keys
end

# "channel(s) added: x; other key(s) changed: repo" for one entry's edit.
def entry_change(before, after)
  was = channels_of(before)
  now = channels_of(after)
  changed = (now.keys & was.keys).reject { |k| now[k] == was[k] }
  others = ((before.keys | after.keys) - ["channels"]).sort.reject { |k| before[k] == after[k] }
  others << "channels (not an object)" if before["channels"] != after["channels"] && was == now
  [["channel(s) added", now.keys - was.keys], ["channel(s) removed", was.keys - now.keys],
   ["channel(s) changed", changed], ["other key(s) changed", others]]
    .reject { |_, names| names.empty? }
    .map { |what, names| "#{what}: #{names.join(', ')}" }
    .join("; ")
end

def report_pending(pending, out = $stdout)
  return if pending.empty?

  out.puts "  #{pending.size} change(s) this branch makes to #{REGISTRY_REL} (pending, not a failure):"
  pending.each { |m| out.puts "  ~ #{m}" }
  out.puts "  After the branch lands, provision them with `scripts/setup-inbox-registry --install` " \
           "from the MAIN checkout. Not before: the live registry is judged against what landed."
end

# Printed with every unreadable landed bar. The check needs origin to know
# which entries landed, before it looks for an inbox root at all, so nobody
# should read exit 3 on such a machine as a new defect.
OFFLINE_NOTE = "  Note: the bar is what landed on origin, so an offline machine, or one with no " \
               "inbox that cannot reach origin, exits 3 (could not measure), never 0."

# Who may run the installer a Fix: names. The gate runs in every captain's
# worktree, so without this a captain that hit drift mid-gate could follow the
# Fix: and edit machine state unasked (the DND-864 fix3 class, 2026-09-28).
INSTALLER_WHO = "Who runs it: a session on this machine that its own owner turn or its own " \
                "admiral's brief authorizes (~/.claude/CLAUDE.md -> Owner approval policy -> " \
                "Notify after). A captain or other subagent without that brief reports it to its " \
                "admiral instead and does not run the installer."

# The newer origin/main's entries, as [description, entries], or nil when
# there is no pin or origin's main is the pin (see Landed.newer_tip). Raises
# Landed::Unreadable, Landed::Mismatch or InboxRegistry::Error.
def newer_entries(root = InboxRegistry.repo_dir)
  tip = Landed.newer_tip(root)
  return nil unless tip

  label, sha = tip
  where = "#{REGISTRY_REL} @ #{label} #{sha[0, 12]}"
  text = Landed.file_at(root, sha, REGISTRY_REL, label)
  [where, text ? InboxRegistry.parse(text, where) : []]
end

# Splits the pinned bar's entries by whether the live entry is AHEAD of it:
# it differs from the pinned declaration and equals the newer origin/main's
# declaration for the same file. Returns [effective, ahead, note]: effective is
# the bar with each ahead entry replaced by its newer declaration (so drift()
# still checks its mode, file type and repo identity), ahead the file names,
# note the newer bar described when something is ahead, else a note saying
# what was checked (nil only when there is no newer origin/main). Any failure to
# read the newer declaration leaves the pinned bar as it is, and says so.
def ahead_of_pin(entries, newer)
  got = newer.call
  return [entries, [], nil] if got.nil?

  desc, newer_list = got
  by_file = newer_list.to_h { |p| [p["file"], p["entry"]] }
  ahead = entries.filter_map do |p|
    want = by_file[p["file"]]
    p["file"] if want && want != p["entry"] && InboxRegistry.live_entry(p["file"]) == want
  end
  effective = entries.map { |p| ahead.include?(p["file"]) ? p.merge("entry" => by_file[p["file"]]) : p }
  return [effective, ahead, desc] unless ahead.empty?

  # Looked and found nothing is said, so it never reads like "did not look".
  [entries, [], "checked #{desc}: no drifting live entry equals its declaration there, so none is " \
                "ahead of the pinned bar"]
rescue Landed::Unreadable, Landed::Mismatch, InboxRegistry::Error => e
  [entries, [], "could not read a newer origin/main to tell whether the live registry is ahead of the " \
                "pinned bar (#{e.message}); it is measured against the pinned bar alone"]
end

# Names each ahead entry (or the note on why none could be judged ahead).
def report_ahead(ahead, desc, out = $stdout)
  return if desc.nil?
  return out.puts("  note: #{desc}") if ahead.empty?

  out.puts "  #{ahead.size} live entr#{ahead.size == 1 ? 'y is' : 'ies are'} ahead of the pinned bar " \
           "(not drift): #{ahead.size == 1 ? 'it equals' : 'each equals'} what #{desc} declares, a commit " \
           "that landed after harness-gate pinned origin/main:"
  ahead.each { |f| out.puts "  ~ #{f}: ahead of the pinned bar" }
end

def unmeasured(lines)
  warn "check-inbox-registry: COULD NOT MEASURE — this is not a pass."
  lines.each { |l| warn l }
  EXIT_UNMEASURED
end

# The check. `landed` is how the landed registry is read (origin, via Landed);
# the inline self-test injects it so that suite stays hermetic.
def run(landed: -> { landed_entries }, newer: -> { newer_entries })
  begin
    branch = InboxRegistry.declared
  rescue InboxRegistry::Error => e
    warn "check-inbox-registry: FAIL — this branch's registry cannot be used: #{e.message}"
    warn "Fix: repair #{REGISTRY_REL} on this branch (`git restore #{REGISTRY_REL}` to start over): " \
         "it is an object with a \"projects\" array of " \
         "{\"file\": \"<name>.json\", \"entry\": {\"v\":1,\"repo\":\"~/dev/<p>/.git\",\"channels\":{}}}."
    return EXIT_MALFORMED
  end
  note = InboxRegistry.validation_note

  bar, entries = measure_landed(landed)
  return unmeasured(entries + [OFFLINE_NOTE]) if bar.nil?

  pending = pending_changes(branch, entries)

  unless File.directory?(InboxRegistry.root)
    # "No root" means one of two very different things, and conflating them is
    # how the whole registry disappears quietly. If a LANDED entry's repo is
    # checked out here, this IS the machine the committed list describes and the
    # root should exist — so its absence is drift. Otherwise there is genuinely
    # nothing to assert. The landed list, never the branch's: a branch that
    # deleted the entry proving this is the machine would otherwise pass.
    if InboxRegistry.declared_repo_present?(entries)
      warn "check-inbox-registry: FAIL — the inbox root #{InboxRegistry.root} does not exist, " \
           "but this machine has a checkout of a repo the #{bar} declares, so it is " \
           "the machine that list describes."
      warn "Fix: run `scripts/setup-inbox-registry --install` from the MAIN checkout to recreate " \
           "the root and the declared entries. If this machine should no longer be a tenant, " \
           "remove its entry from #{REGISTRY_REL} and land that."
      warn INSTALLER_WHO
      report_pending(pending, $stderr)
      return EXIT_FAIL
    end
    puts "check-inbox-registry: no inbox root at #{InboxRegistry.root} and no repo the #{bar} " \
         "declares is checked out here — nothing to assert (not this environment). OK."
    report_pending(pending)
    return EXIT_OK
  end

  problems = InboxRegistry.drift(entries)
  ahead = []
  ahead_desc = nil
  unless problems.empty?
    # Only on drift: a pass against the pinned bar needs no newer read.
    effective, ahead, ahead_desc = ahead_of_pin(entries, newer)
    problems = InboxRegistry.drift(effective) unless ahead.empty?
  end
  if problems.empty?
    puts "check-inbox-registry: all #{entries.size} landed registry " \
         "entr#{entries.size == 1 ? 'y' : 'ies'} #{entries.size == 1 ? 'is' : 'are'} installed and " \
         "#{entries.size == 1 ? 'matches' : 'match'} the #{bar}#{ahead.empty? ? '' : ', or is ahead of it'}. OK." +
         (note ? " (#{note})" : "")
    report_ahead(ahead, ahead_desc)
    report_pending(pending)
    return EXIT_OK
  end

  warn "check-inbox-registry: FAIL — #{problems.size} registry problem(s) under #{InboxRegistry.projects_dir} " \
       "(bar: #{bar}):"
  problems.each { |p| warn "  - #{p}" }
  warn "  note: #{note}" if note
  report_ahead(ahead, ahead_desc, $stderr)
  warn "Fix: run `scripts/setup-inbox-registry --install` from the MAIN checkout, up to date with " \
       "origin/main, to re-materialise the landed entries (it writes only the entries it " \
       "declares, backs up anything it replaces, and never touches another entry " \
       "in projects/). If an entry was intentionally retired or its channels " \
       "changed, edit #{REGISTRY_REL}, land it, and re-run the installer — " \
       "the committed file is the source of truth, and a live entry that exists " \
       "nowhere in git is exactly the state this check exists to prevent. A change " \
       "only this branch makes is listed as pending below and is never the cause."
  warn INSTALLER_WHO
  report_pending(pending, $stderr)
  EXIT_FAIL
end

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
def self_test
  require "tmpdir"
  require "fileutils"
  require "json"

  ok = true
  check = lambda do |name, cond|
    puts "  #{cond ? 'ok  ' : 'FAIL'} #{name}"
    ok &&= cond
  end

  quiet = lambda do |&blk|
    o, e = $stdout, $stderr
    $stdout = $stderr = File.open(File::NULL, "w")
    begin
      blk.call
    ensure
      $stdout.close
      $stdout, $stderr = o, e
    end
  end

  capture = lambda do |&blk|
    require "stringio"
    o, e = $stdout, $stderr
    buf = StringIO.new
    $stdout = $stderr = buf
    begin
      blk.call
    ensure
      $stdout, $stderr = o, e
    end
    buf.string
  end

  Dir.mktmpdir("check-inbox-registry-selftest") do |dir|
    # A source of truth that names a repo NOT present on this machine, so the
    # git cross-check is inert and each case isolates one property.
    src = File.join(dir, "registry.json")
    entry = { "v" => 1, "repo" => File.join(dir, "nowhere", ".git"),
              "channels" => { "demo" => { "kind" => "log", "path" => "demo.jsonl" } } }
    File.write(src, JSON.pretty_generate({ "projects" => [{ "file" => "demo.json", "entry" => entry }] }))
    ENV["ATHENA_INBOX_REGISTRY"] = src

    root = File.join(dir, "root")
    ENV["ATHENA_INBOX_ROOT"] = root

    # The landed bar is injected so this suite stays hermetic: by default the
    # branch copy (src) stands in for what landed. The origin-backed read is
    # proven end to end, on fixture repos with a bare origin, by
    # ai/test/check-inbox-registry/self-test.sh.
    as_landed = ->(file) { -> { ["fixture landed #{File.basename(file)}", InboxRegistry.parse(File.read(file), file)] } }
    no_newer = -> {}
    go = ->(landed = as_landed.call(src), newer = no_newer) { quiet.call { run(landed: landed, newer: newer) } }

    # 1. Absent root -> not this environment, exit 0. (Env-safety: the check
    #    must never false-fail a machine that does not run the facility.)
    check.call("absent root -> exit 0", go.call == 0)

    # 2. Root present, projects/ absent -> drift, exit 1. (The opposite of the
    #    case above: the facility IS here, so a missing registry is real.)
    FileUtils.mkdir_p(root)
    File.chmod(0o700, root)
    check.call("root without projects/ -> exit 1", go.call == 1)

    # 3. A correctly installed entry -> clean.
    projects = File.join(root, "projects")
    FileUtils.mkdir_p(projects)
    File.chmod(0o700, projects)
    path = File.join(projects, "demo.json")
    File.write(path, InboxRegistry.render(entry))
    File.chmod(0o600, path)
    check.call("installed entry -> no drift", InboxRegistry.drift.empty?)

    # 4. An entry edited by hand -> drift naming the file and the key.
    File.write(path, InboxRegistry.render(entry.merge("channels" => {})))
    File.chmod(0o600, path)
    d = InboxRegistry.drift
    check.call("hand-edited entry -> drift names it", d.size == 1 && d.first.include?("demo.json") && d.first.include?("channels"))
    # The Fix: names who may run the installer, so a captain that hits it
    # mid-gate reports instead of editing machine state (DND-864 fix3).
    check.call("drift Fix: says a subagent reports it to its admiral",
               capture.call { run(landed: as_landed.call(src), newer: no_newer) }.include?("reports it to its admiral"))

    # 5. A wrong file mode is drift on its own (0600 is a contract MUST).
    File.write(path, InboxRegistry.render(entry))
    File.chmod(0o644, path)
    d = InboxRegistry.drift
    check.call("0644 entry -> mode drift", d.size == 1 && d.first.include?("0644"))

    # 6. A wrong directory mode is drift too (0700 is a contract MUST).
    File.chmod(0o600, path)
    File.chmod(0o755, projects)
    d = InboxRegistry.drift
    check.call("0755 projects/ -> mode drift", d.size == 1 && d.first.include?("0755"))
    File.chmod(0o700, projects)

    # 7. A deleted entry -> drift naming it.
    FileUtils.rm_f(path)
    d = InboxRegistry.drift
    check.call("deleted entry -> drift names it", d.size == 1 && d.first.include?("demo.json"))

    # 8. An unrelated entry in projects/ is never named. It is not ours to
    #    police, and naming it would make this check a tenant-disclosure path.
    File.write(File.join(projects, "someone_else.json"), "{}")
    check.call("unrelated entry is not named", InboxRegistry.drift.none? { |p| p.include?("someone_else") })

    # 9. A 0755 inbox ROOT is drift too, not only a 0755 projects/. Every
    #    directory under the root MUST be 0700, and a listable root exposes
    #    every tenant's message surfaces.
    File.write(path, InboxRegistry.render(entry))
    File.chmod(0o600, path)
    File.chmod(0o755, root)
    d = InboxRegistry.drift
    check.call("0755 root -> mode drift", d.size == 1 && d.first.include?("inbox root"))
    File.chmod(0o700, root)

    # 10. A symlink where an entry belongs is reported as what it is, never
    #     followed. Following it is how an installer ends up writing outside the
    #     root entirely.
    FileUtils.rm_f(path)
    File.symlink(File.join(dir, "elsewhere.json"), path)
    d = InboxRegistry.drift
    check.call("symlinked entry -> reported, not followed",
               d.size == 1 && d.first.include?("not a regular file"))
    FileUtils.rm_f(path)

    # 11. Two declared entries claiming one repo identity is the reader's own
    #     hard error, so the committed list is refused outright (exit 2) rather
    #     than installed into a wedged state.
    dupe = { "projects" => [{ "file" => "a.json", "entry" => entry },
                            { "file" => "b.json", "entry" => entry }] }
    File.write(src, JSON.pretty_generate(dupe))
    check.call("two entries claiming one repo -> exit 2", go.call == 2)

    # 12. An absent root is NOT "not this environment" when a declared repo is
    #     checked out here: that proves this is the machine the committed list
    #     describes, so the missing root is drift. Without this discriminator,
    #     losing the whole root reads as OK.
    here = { "v" => 1, "repo" => InboxRegistry.git_common_dir(InboxRegistry.repo_dir), "channels" => {} }
    File.write(src, JSON.pretty_generate({ "projects" => [{ "file" => "here.json", "entry" => here }] }))
    FileUtils.rm_rf(root)
    check.call("absent root + a declared repo checked out here -> exit 1", go.call == 1)
    check.call("absent-root Fix: says a subagent reports it to its admiral",
               capture.call { run(landed: as_landed.call(src), newer: no_newer) }.include?("reports it to its admiral"))

    # 13. A malformed source of truth exits 2 (a code error, not machine state).
    File.write(src, "{ not json")
    check.call("malformed source of truth -> exit 2", go.call == 2)

    # 14-19. THE BAR IS WHAT LANDED (DND-792). The live registry holds exactly
    #        the landed entry; the branch copy (src) differs from it.
    landed_src = File.join(dir, "landed.json")
    File.write(landed_src, JSON.pretty_generate({ "projects" => [{ "file" => "demo.json", "entry" => entry }] }))
    landed = as_landed.call(landed_src)
    FileUtils.mkdir_p(projects)
    File.chmod(0o700, root)
    File.chmod(0o700, projects)
    File.write(path, InboxRegistry.render(entry))
    File.chmod(0o600, path)
    peer = entry.merge("repo" => File.join(dir, "nowhere-peer", ".git"))
    File.write(src, JSON.pretty_generate({ "projects" => [{ "file" => "demo.json", "entry" => entry },
                                                          { "file" => "peer.json", "entry" => peer }] }))
    check.call("a branch-added entry, not installed, is pending -> exit 0", go.call(landed) == 0)
    pend = pending_changes(InboxRegistry.declared, InboxRegistry.parse(File.read(landed_src), landed_src))
    check.call("...and is named as pending", pend.size == 1 && pend.first.start_with?("peer.json: a new entry"))

    wider = entry.merge("channels" => entry["channels"].merge("extra" => { "kind" => "log", "path" => "extra.jsonl" }))
    File.write(src, JSON.pretty_generate({ "projects" => [{ "file" => "demo.json", "entry" => wider }] }))
    pend = pending_changes(InboxRegistry.declared, InboxRegistry.parse(File.read(landed_src), landed_src))
    check.call("a branch-added channel is pending, named -> exit 0",
               go.call(landed) == 0 && pend == ["demo.json: channel(s) added: extra"])

    File.write(src, JSON.pretty_generate({ "projects" => [] }))
    FileUtils.rm_f(path)
    check.call("a landed entry the branch retires, deleted live -> still drift, exit 1", go.call(landed) == 1)

    unreadable = -> { raise Landed::Unreadable.new([["fixture probe", "unreachable"]]) }
    check.call("landed bar unreadable -> exit 3", go.call(unreadable) == 3)
    mismatch = -> { raise Landed::Mismatch.new("a" * 40, "b" * 40) }
    check.call("local origin/main disagrees with origin -> exit 3", go.call(mismatch) == 3)

    # 20-23. AHEAD OF THE PINNED BAR (DND-1552). The live entry equals what a
    #        newer origin/main declares; the pinned (landed) bar differs. The
    #        origin-backed read is proven end to end by
    #        ai/test/check-inbox-registry/self-test.sh.
    File.write(src, JSON.pretty_generate({ "projects" => [{ "file" => "demo.json", "entry" => entry }] }))
    File.write(path, InboxRegistry.render(wider))
    File.chmod(0o600, path)
    newer_of = ->(e) { -> { ["fixture newer", [{ "file" => "demo.json", "entry" => e }]] } }
    check.call("live entry equals the newer declaration -> exit 0", go.call(landed, newer_of.call(wider)) == 0)
    check.call("...and it is named as ahead of the pinned bar",
               capture.call { run(landed: landed, newer: newer_of.call(wider)) }
                 .include?("demo.json: ahead of the pinned bar"))
    check.call("live entry equals neither declaration -> still drift, exit 1",
               go.call(landed, newer_of.call(entry.merge("channels" => {}))) == 1)
    unread_newer = -> { raise Landed::Unreadable.new([["fixture probe", "unreachable"]]) }
    check.call("newer origin/main unreadable -> the pinned drift stands, exit 1, and says so",
               go.call(landed, unread_newer) == 1 &&
               capture.call { run(landed: landed, newer: unread_newer) }.include?("could not read a newer origin/main"))
  end

  # 10. Repo identity resolves at the point of capture: this repo's common dir
  #     comes back ABSOLUTE even though git prints `.git` in a main checkout.
  #     Resolving that raw string later is the trap that silently yields zero
  #     channels; a helper returning a relative path would fail here.
  common = InboxRegistry.git_common_dir(InboxRegistry.repo_dir)
  check.call("git common dir is absolute and ends in .git",
             !common.nil? && common.start_with?("/") && File.basename(common) == ".git")

  # 11. A non-git directory is not a fault — nil, never a raise.
  Dir.mktmpdir { |d| check.call("non-git dir -> nil", InboxRegistry.git_common_dir(d).nil?) }

  ENV.delete("ATHENA_INBOX_REGISTRY")
  ENV.delete("ATHENA_INBOX_ROOT")

  puts(ok ? "ALL CASES PASS" : "SELF-TEST FAILED")
  unless ok
    warn "Fix: repair the drift logic in ai/inbox/lib/registry.rb (or this " \
         "self-test's expectations if a rule genuinely changed) until every " \
         "case above passes; a broken checker is worse than none, because the " \
         "gate then reports PASS over a dead registry."
  end
  ok ? 0 : 1
end

if ARGV.include?("--help") || ARGV.include?("-h")
  puts <<~TXT
    Usage:
      ai/bin/check-inbox-registry              assert this machine's Athena Inbox
                                               tenancy entries under
                                               $ATHENA_INBOX_ROOT/projects/ match
                                               ai/inbox/registry.json AS LANDED on
                                               origin/main; what only this branch
                                               changes there is named as pending
                                               (not a failure). Exit 0 ok, 1 drift,
                                               2 malformed branch registry, 3 could
                                               not measure the landed registry
      ai/bin/check-inbox-registry --self-test  deterministic suite (no model)
      ai/bin/check-inbox-registry --help       this text

    Environment-safe: passes with a note when there is no inbox root and no
    landed entry's repo is checked out here (CI/agent env). Recover drift with
    `scripts/setup-inbox-registry --install` from the main checkout.
  TXT
  exit 0
end
if ARGV.include?("--self-test")
  exit self_test
elsif ARGV.empty?
  exit run
else
  warn "check-inbox-registry: unknown argument(s): #{ARGV.join(' ')}"
  warn "Fix: run it with no arguments to check the live registry, or with --self-test."
  exit 1
end
